    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0115" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg33"/>

                <head>Mr. Motley to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 10, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the circular of date June 7, ultimo, signed by yourself, giving notice of the
                    departure of Admiral Goldsborough to take command of the European squadron, and
                    communicating certain orders of the Navy Department to that officer.</p>
                <p>As you are well aware, those orders have no particular application, so far as the
                    ports of this empire are concerned, the imperial government never having
                    extended belligerent rights to United States rebels.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. LOTHROP MOTLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
